module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.shared_grant_dropin_overwritten

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data shared_grant_dropin_overwritten: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "shared_grant_dropin_overwritten" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**one drop-in file for a parameterized grant, so each install overwrites the last** (every InspectServingContainer grant was written to /etc/sudoers.d/gunbc-docker-inspect, so granting a second container revoked the first, and each install's readback confirmed only its own line).",

    "INVALID STATE: gunbc.spark.managed_grant_reconcile spark_managed_grant_dropin_name mapped every InspectServingContainer { container } to one name, so the file a grant writes did not vary with the grant's parameter.",

    "HARM: Group A srv5, fleet-converge run 37166203531: the pair, native and staircase inspect grants all wrote the same file; only the last container stayed inspectable, and serving observation for the others refused for want of a grant the receipts said had been installed. Group B (srv9..srv12) still reads in the shared shape on 2026-10-04 22:53Z: the shared file present and no per-container file, so exactly one container is grantable there and which one is unread.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a parameterized grant whose drop-in name omits the parameter; sudo's own listing cannot attribute an entry to a file, so the shape is read from the drop-in NAMES (gunbc.spark.managed_grant_reconcile spark_inspect_dropin_shape_of_names).",

    "RUNG: found at 1. Now 3 for the install: the drop-in name carries the container (gunbc#13040), so two grants writing one file has no constructor. The ON-HOST state left by the old shape is a coverage obligation, not assumed: gunbc.fleet_multi_principal_probe spark_grant_coverage names every procured Spark as probed, hand-read or unobserved, and the probe reads each probed host's drop-in shape. CEILING 3 for the residue too. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an operator-approved converge that installs the per-container drop-ins on Group B and removes the shared file, with a readback of the names, SUFFICIENT FOR no procured Spark reading SharedInspectDropinShape.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
